    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620-a3">

                <pb facs="1091" n="997" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg997"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 to inclosure in No.
                    198.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Hidalgo &amp; Co.
                        to Mr. Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 22,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to your valued communication of
                    the 21st instant, we beg to say that we have often been warned by the inspector
                    of police for the bay not to issue any tickets of passage without a passport or
                    a consular certificate duly visaed by the civil government, unless we were
                    willing by so doing to expose the parties holding such tickets to be withdrawn
                    from on board the ship and ourselves to be fined.</p>
                <p>This is what we have to state in reference to the object of your inquiry, and beg
                    to subscribe ourselves, sir, very respectfully, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hidalgo &amp; Co.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
